er G-D1, G-D2, G-D2b; G-D3 red for ROUND-1 and HEAD by the helper message, rows reaching the delayed line; G-D4 row 3 red by the helper message at about 3 s for ROUND-1 and HEAD. Print per run: filter, the count that RAN (> 0), red rows by name, the failing message text, elapsed. Controls per tree: **c0** (unmutated: ran 3 on OLD, ran 3 on ROUND-1, ran 6 on HEAD, 0 red), **c1** (trailing comment appended), **c2** (equivalent whitespace). **Under load:** no artificial CPU hog, ever (the delay mutants stand in); print `uptime` load1 beside every run and say the real load was other seats' jobs. (d) The cost of the settle: quiet-run elapsed of the b116 file at HEAD against ROUND-1 (expected about +0.3 s for three rows of 100 ms), in `-probe` as a one-off measure. If a quiet HEAD run needs more than 2000 ms for the file, say so and grade nothing without a reason.
